# npm install flags shared between local dev and Cloudflare Pages builds.
#
# Cloudflare Pages detects package-lock.json and runs `npm ci` instead of
# `npm install`. `npm ci` is strict — peer-dependency warnings that the local
# `npm install` (npm 11) tolerates become hard errors and abort the build in
# 3-4 seconds before vite ever runs.
#
# `legacy-peer-deps=true` keeps the historically-loose behavior of npm 6/7
# for both `npm install` and `npm ci`, so the project's peer dep conflicts
# (h3 / ocache from nitro 3 beta) are warnings, not failures.
#
# Without this file, Cloudflare Pages build aborts:
#   clone_repo ✓ 2s
#   build      ✗ 3.6s  -> "npm ci" aborts on peer-dep validation
#
# See: https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/npmrc
legacy-peer-deps=true
